  "status_text": "A simple rule just came back checked: cutting a graph down never makes it harder. Checked in Lean, on one-a-side inputs: keep any rows and columns of a bipartite graph, and the kept graph has a fan-in-two AND/OR/NOT circuit no larger than the whole graph's [L-meta-23955]. So a hard piece found inside a big graph is a floor for the whole graph too, our reading of the row. Verdicts and merges are slower this hour; everything sent is kept.",
